      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19682\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qenter.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_19682\u0026quot;,144)\"\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e",
      "figure": null,
      "figures": null
    },
    {
      "role": "step",
      "content": "\u003cdiv class\u003d\"step_content\"\u003e\n \u003cp\u003ePress \u003cimg id\u003d\"token_19683\" class\u003d\"text-bottom\" src\u003d\"/specialchars/qenter.gif\" onmouseout\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOut()\" onmouseover\u003d\"return parent.doMouseOver(\u0026quot;token_19683\u0026quot;,144)\"\u003e. The calculator finds the distances from each point to \u003ci\u003eA\u003c/i\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eThe smallest value is 3.6056, corresponding to the point \u003ci\u003eE\u003c/i\u003e(6, 4). So, this is the closest point to \u003ci\u003eA\u003c/i\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003eThe largest value is 7, corresponding to the point \u003ci\u003eF\u003c/i\u003e(3, 9). This is the farthest point from \u003ci\u003eA\u003c/i\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n \u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cimg class\u003d\"graphimgstatic id\u003d\" figure-9 src\u003d\"/modules/gcprealgpractice/gcprealgpractice_8_1_realnumbersandthepythagoreantheorem_5_70/f-70-5-4.gif\"\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e",
